t/pull/122519#issuecomment-6179643469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122519","id":6179643469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcFXgTQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T22:12:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T22:37:11Z","body":"Perhaps the wording of the PR's title should be improved. Previously, only the first statement after a `return` was given the `UNREACHABLE_CODE` warning; this PR expands it to every statement logically following the `return`.\r\n\r\nWhile code inside an `if false:` block would also be logically unreachable, the warning does not currently trigger for that case, and as such it wouldn't trigger with this PR either. Here's a screenshot of some unreachable code in VS Code with the language server from current master:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"414\" height=\"256\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-10-14 at 3 11 05 PM@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec1a404f-fd75-493a-89a7-d8ac2d5a6d89\" />\r\n\r\nNote that the `print(\"this is unreachable\")` code on line 6 is the only one highlighted since it comes after a return; even though `print(\"can't get here\")` on line 12 is logically unreachable, the warning doesn't trigger for it.\r\n\r\nThis would be something to tackle in a separate PR, I think.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6179643469/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6186056378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122519#issuecomment-6186056378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122519","id":6186056378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcLe6ug","user":{"login":"notroid5","id":87585310,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg1MzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87585310?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5","html_url":"https://github.com/notroid5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notroid5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:34:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T06:08:39Z","body":"I see, that seems indeed out of scope then. But what about code after `continue`/`break`?\r\n\r\nEdit: Opened proposal for `if/while false` (and more): https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15648","author_associ